{
  "projects": [
    {
      "name": "example-project",
      "path": "/absolute/path/to/project",
      "type": "python",
      "environment": {},
      "commands": {
        "status": ["git", "status", "--short"],
        "test": ["python", "-m", "pytest"],
        "lint": ["python", "-m", "ruff", "check", "."]
      },
      "timeouts": {"test": 900, "lint": 300}
    }
  ]
}

Commands should use argv arrays so argument text is passed literally without
shell interpretation. Legacy strings are accepted only with `"trusted_shell": true`
on the individual project; that explicitly opts into executing trusted local shell
code when `--execute` is used. Treat project configuration and environment values
as executable-code inputs.
